      "writtenOn": "2017-03-22T02:21:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking through existing code, it seems like there are several different ways of checking the status of filesystem encryption:\n\n- [dexopt.cpp]\n  vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"trigger_restart_min_framework\" ||\n    vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"1\" \n- [BootAnimation.cpp]\n  atoi(vold_decrypt) !\u003d 0 ||\n    vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"trigger_restart_min_framework\" \n- [UsbDebuggingManager.java]\n  vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"trigger_restart_min_framework\" \n- [EncryptionHelper.java]\n  vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"1\" ||\n    vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"trigger_restart_min_framework\" \n- [SystemServer.java]\n  vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"trigger_restart_min_framework\" || \n    vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"1\" \n- [UiccController.java]\n  vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"trigger_restart_framework\" \n- [StorageManager.java]\n  vold_decrypt \u003d\u003d \"trigger_restart_min_framework\" \n\nIt seems the check for DEVICE_ENCRYPTING matches the consensus of existing code (only one piece of existing code goes the other way).\n\nBut DEVICE_ENCRYPTED seems to be unique to this new code. The existing code seems to check for \"1\", instead. \n\nGiven this, maybe:\n- We should have DEVICE_ENCRYPTED be \"1\", rather than \"trigger_reset_main\"?\n- Or perhaps we can use the same constants and logic as in SystemServer.java? (The hope here would be that, if this logic ever changes, someone modifying SystemServer might grep the rest of the tree, and do us a solid.)",
      "revId": "e0b9d83108aa35004541c84bc57e4ee10f81b775",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
